			<div class="content" id="post-content-2783429">
									

<p>If I'm following you now, you are using the In­ter­me­di­ate Value The­o­rem on the function of possible messages, not possible lottery numbers. I had thought it was the winning numbers. So, then</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The winning number is 12345678</p>
</blockquote>
<p>and</p>
<blockquote>
<p>12345678 is the winning number</p>
</blockquote>
<p>are counted as different messages in the function.<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-121915-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-121915-1')">1</a></sup><br />
The differences in the message sent create a repeatable, but unpredictable change in the timestream. The same message would always create the same change, but that's impossible to predict from your reference point, and it's impossible to return to your reference point once you try it.<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-121915-2" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-121915-2')">2</a></sup> The In­ter­me­di­ate Value The­o­rem does then apply.<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-121915-3" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-121915-3')">3</a></sup></p>
<p>I'm hoping to see an explanation for why people don't just auto-send random gibberish back every time something bad happens. (Maybe that's what's happening at <a href="/scp-176">SCP-176</a>, one of my favorites)</p>
<div class="footnotes-footer">
<div class="title">Footnotes</div>
<div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-121915-1"><a href="javascript:;" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnoteref-121915-1')">1</a>. and converted into an all number format, like binary, to make this easier</div>
<div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-121915-2"><a href="javascript:;" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnoteref-121915-2')">2</a>. From your previous chapter.</div>
<div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-121915-3"><a href="javascript:;" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnoteref-121915-3')">3</a>. more or less. I'm still a little unsure about the need to also send the information necessary to win. You'd need to include the winning lottery number in any message, and it's unclear to me if that would violate a Darboux function.</div>
</div>

